---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/card.css";
import "../styles/result.css";
---

<Base title="Build your tags" description="Paste a briefing file, see it checked as you type, and copy Open Briefing Standard tags for your site, your CMS or your feed." path="/build">
  <div class="prose intro">
    <h1>Build your tags</h1>
    <p class="lede">Paste a briefing file. It is checked as you type, and the tags come out escaped and ready for your site.</p>
  </div>

  <form id="build-form" class="builder" novalidate>
    <label for="build-file">Your briefing file</label>
    <textarea id="build-file" name="file" spellcheck="true" rows="16" placeholder="summary: |&#10;  Your summary of the post, in plain text.&#10;headline: One or two lines to hear before going further.&#10;status: draft"></textarea>
    <p class="note">
      Nothing you type leaves this page. No file yet?{" "}<button type="button" class="linkish" id="build-example">Start from an example</button>,{" "}or{" "}<a href="/publish#draft">have your assistant draft one</a>.
    </p>

    <details class="paste">
      <summary>Check the highlights against your post</summary>
      <p class="note">A highlight is a passage copied from the post, word for word. Paste the post's text and each one is looked up in it.</p>
      <label for="build-post" class="visually-hidden">The post's text</label>
      <textarea id="build-post" name="post" spellcheck="false" placeholder="The post's text"></textarea>
      <p>
        <button type="button" class="quiet" id="build-fetch">Read it from the post's address</button>
      </p>
      <p id="build-fetch-note" class="note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="note">This reads the address in the file's <code>url:</code> line through the same helper the checker uses. Only the address is sent.</p>
    </details>
    <p id="build-status" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </form>

  <div id="build-result" class="result"></div>

  <section id="build-output" class="output" hidden>
    <h2>Your tags</h2>
    <p id="build-draft" class="draft-note" hidden>
      This is a draft, and the tags say so. Once you have read every line and it says what you mean:{" "}<button type="button" class="linkish" id="build-approve">mark it approved</button>.
    </p>
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Where the tags are going"></div>
    <div id="build-panel" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0">
      <p id="build-note" class="note"></p>
      <pre><code id="build-code"></code></pre>
      <p id="build-copy"></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <noscript><p class="prose">The builder runs in your browser and needs JavaScript. Without it, use <code>npx openbriefing tags your-file.yaml</code>.</p></noscript>

  <div class="prose after">
    <h2>The briefing file</h2>
    <p>
      A briefing file is a few lines of YAML. Only <code>summary</code> is needed. A wrapped line is read as a space, and a
      blank line as a paragraph break.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>What to write</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>summary</code></td><td>Your summary. Around 200 to 350 words serves the most uses.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>headline</code></td><td>One or two lines, 40 words or fewer.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>keep</code></td><td>Up to three lines every shorter version should keep. The first is the core message.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>highlights</code></td><td>Up to five passages from the post that may be quoted on their own, each with an optional <code>label</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>attribution</code></td><td>How to credit you, such as "From Example Blog".</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>url</code></td><td>The post's address.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>status</code></td><td><code>draft</code> until you have read every line, then <code>approved</code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Also read: <code>title</code>, <code>summary_short</code>, <code>summary_long</code>, <code>derive</code>, <code>translate</code>,{" "}<code>combine</code>, <code>preference</code>, <code>lang</code> and <code>modified</code>. Each matches{" "}<a href="/ns">the tag of the same name</a>.
    </p>
    <p>The same file works from the command line:</p>
    <pre><code>npx openbriefing tags your-file.yaml</code></pre>
  </div>
</Base>

<script src="../scripts/builder.ts"></script>

<style is:global>
  .intro h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.4rem + 3.4vw, 3.6rem);
  }
  .intro .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .builder {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .builder > label {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .builder #build-file {
    min-height: 20rem;
  }
  .builder .note {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }
  .linkish {
    all: unset;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--pencil);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }
  .linkish:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--pencil);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .builder .paste {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .builder .paste > summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .builder .paste textarea {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
  }
  .builder .paste p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .result .state {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--slate);
  }
  .output {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .output > * + * {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .output .draft-note {
    border-left: 6px solid var(--marker);
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
  }
  .tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .tabs button {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1.5px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 0;
    border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .tabs button:hover {
    background: var(--wash);
    color: var(--ink);
    border-color: transparent;
  }
  .tabs button[aria-selected="true"] {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }
  #build-panel > * + * {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }
  #build-panel pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    max-height: 26rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }
  .after {
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }
</style>
